From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:56:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] gl: MMPX-upscaled HUD textures, and shader programs linked
 ahead of their first draw from a recorded list

HUD upscaling (ui_upscale, on): a small texture that only through-mode draws sample and that looks like pixel art (a palette
texture, or at most 256 colours) is uploaded at twice its size, made by MMPX (host/gpu/mmpx.{hpp,cpp}, after McGuire and Gagiu,
JCGT 2021, via Yakumo's MIT code; credit in docs/SOURCE_PROVENANCE.md). The guest's texture, size register and coordinates are
unchanged. The pass is a CPU pass once per texture and is metered: ui_upscale_budget_us (1500) is what a frame may spend after the
first pass, ui_upscale_max_us (3000) leaves a texture alone when the earlier passes predict a longer one; a texture over budget is
drawn as the original and done at a later frame. Mip building skips these textures.

Shader pre-link (prewarm, on): every program the renderer links is appended to <data>/shader_variants.txt (header
"# portablekit-gl-variants 1"); a shipped <data>/shader_cache/variants.txt is read too. warm_up_step() links the listed programs one
per call while the GL thread has nothing to draw (all at once during boot, later only after a 20 ms lull). variant_dir moves the
folder; prewarm=0 reads and writes no list. A list is only a hint: a flag set that cannot be built is skipped.

ge_replay --stats prints the ui2x counters. docs/GL_RENDERER.md describes both, and the decode paragraph of the previous commit.

Verified on x86-64 (software GL): HUD frames of mission 1 with and without ui_upscale differ only in the HUD (icons and frames
crisper, the minimap ring thinner); two bot runs of the same data folder: the first recorded 25 programs, the second linked all 25
during boot and linked none at a draw. The MMPX unit test passes; framework tests 45 of 45.
Not verified: the cost of an MMPX pass or of a link on the PS Vita (the budgets are guesses until measured there), whether the
shipped shader cache and list match the build (the Oct 10 cache matches none of the 81 current variants and needs a console to
regenerate).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

